message: "If you use this software or benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "DoubtGate: a doubt-aware retrieval-augmented QA toolkit and benchmark (answer, flag or refuse)"
type: software
version: "0.1.0-dev"
date-released: "2026-10-18"
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: "Arnab"
    family-names: "Khan"
    affiliation: "Novum Labs Pvt. Ltd."
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add the real ORCID iD
  - name: "Novum Labs Pvt. Ltd."
repository-code: "https://github.com/ORG-HANDLE/doubtgate"   # replace ORG-HANDLE with your GitHub handle
abstract: >-
  DoubtGate is an open toolkit and benchmark for deciding when a retrieval-based
  question-answering system should answer, flag or refuse. It targets a small
  physics (quantum mechanics) knowledge base with human-verified labels, and
  measures near-miss questions matched to the wrong stored question and planted
  factual and numeric errors, using CPU-only retrieval baselines and a SymPy
  numeric verifier. Status: pre-alpha, no results yet.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - selective refusal
  - abstention
  - benchmark
  - question answering
  - physics education
